      "title": "chat: add customization migration assessment telemetry",
      "url": "https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/pull/333196",
      "baseSha": "a47dab6a0a5258924b2454f64fc373fc7e657677",
      "headSha": "cd4d9a1f199af5462d0e97190012a87f28eca618",
      "findingCount": 1,
      "published": true,
      "jsonReport": "pr-333196-cd4d9a1f199a.json",
      "markdownReport": "pr-333196-cd4d9a1f199a.md",
      "publishedComments": [
        {
          "path": "src/vs/sessions/services/sessions/browser/sessionsService.ts",
          "line": 939,
          "side": "RIGHT",
          "body": "**[Experimental performance review bot]**\n\n**Severity: medium**\n\nStartup restore now queues a full customization migration assessment for every restored session. Although each enqueue receives the restore cancellation token, queued and running factories discard it once admitted by the limiter.\n\nIf the user opens a session while startup is restoring several persisted sessions—especially while agent/customization state is cold—all stale restore assessments continue in the background. They consume filesystem/extension-provider I/O and MCP assessment CPU after the restore was abandoned, contending with the newly opened session and prolonging post-navigation activity.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Recheck the restore token inside the limiter factory and pass it to `reportCustomizationMigrationTelemetry`; make the MCP assessment wait cancellation-aware as well so already-running work releases its scope promptly. This preserves the concurrency limit and telemetry for restores that remain active while dropping only superseded work.\n\n(Written by Copilot)"
        }
      ]
    },
